只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness 中文多智能体插件「百工」：天枢统筹 12 位专家，证据门禁、多层模型路由与回退、内嵌 Jev 判断工具","id":"gh:1408137745","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-agent-swarm","slug":"zhairy/dsh-agent-swarm","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","multi-agent"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness 中文多智能体插件「百工」：天枢统筹 12 位专家，证据门禁、多层模型路由与回退、内嵌 Jev 判断工具"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-agent-swarm"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"中文 · English"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"### What's new in 3.3.5"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"- Restores validated task and delegation snapshots atomically while retaining strict control, delega"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"tion, and thread identity checks.\n- Adapts cold Session observation and step-scoped tool admission; "},{"id":"p5s3","text":"the model bridge reassembles tools and prompts after a route switch and preserves actual request evi"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"dence.\n- Holds a child model request until its task authorization is bound, with cancellation and sh"},{"id":"p5s5","text":" child model request until its task authorization is bound, with cancellation and shutdown handling."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"### What's new in 3.3.3"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- A model selected explicitly in the DSH picker now outranks task-card risk upgrades. Real quota, au"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"thentication, protocol and network failures still use the bounded fallback chain, without replacing "},{"id":"p7s3","text":"the durable human preference.\n- Restored sessions rebind prompts, personas and tool restrictions fro"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"m the current `agentPreset` projection. A stale child scope is revoked and rebuilt, while Router wri"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"te denial and Worker/worktree boundaries remain enforced.\n- EventJournal state transactions now hold"},{"id":"p7s6","text":" chunked snapshots, encoded changes and commit markers. With `events.journal` enabled, task, delegat"},{"id":"p7s7","text":"ion, binding, control, context, budget, route-health and runtime state survive even when the local `"},{"id":"p7s8","text":"persistence` cache is disabled or deleted.\n- Adds unified Source adapters, immutable Triggers, proac"},{"id":"p7s9","text":"tive `off/observe/auto` decisions, Thread subscriptions and a durable Outbox. Auto mode requires a v"},{"id":"p7s10","text":"alid Mandate; manual follow-ups become Ticket context without a duplicate Eval; fsynced intents resu"},{"id":"p7s11","text":"me through bounded, effect-idempotent handlers."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"### What's new in 3.3.2"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"- Oversized legacy ledger data is migrated as a bounded, redacted, hash-bound summary; non-event jou"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"rnal tails recover without rewriting sealed corruption.\n- Windows uses explicit best-effort director"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"y-entry durability while file sync, rename and other permission failures remain strict.\n- Read-only "},{"id":"p9s4","text":"task projections expose native DSH todos, time context, plan mode, goals, jobs, ask-user and worktre"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"s expose native DSH todos, time context, plan mode, goals, jobs, ask-user and worktree availability."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"### What's new in 3.3.1"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"- Corrects the direct OpenAI API metadata overlay: GPT-6 Astra, GPT-6 Sol, GPT-6.1 Sol, GPT-6 Luna a"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"nd GPT-6.1 Terra use the documented 1.05M context instead of the erroneous 272K long-context pricing"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" boundary.\n- Keeps provider boundaries: Codex/ChatGPT Work and third-party compatible gateways conti"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"nue to use their own reported or subscription-specific limits.\n- Adds `scripts/repair-openai-metadat"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"a.mjs` to inspect an active profile without changes and, with `--apply`, back up and atomically repa"},{"id":"p11s6","text":"ir existing direct OpenAI model entries.\n- Separates context capacity from output capacity in diagno"},{"id":"p11s7","text":"stics: 1.05M context does not mean 1.05M output, and reasoning tokens share the 128K output budget."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### What's new in 3.3.0"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"- Completes the strangler runtime handoff: `service.ts` is now a facade, while host guards, context/"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"mailbox/math/experience queries and DSH subagent adaptation are separate application/adapter modules"},{"id":"p13s3","text":".\n- The committed StateStore snapshot is the sole business-state source. V2 events are synchronized "},{"id":"p13s4","text":"after commit with backups, manifests, approval/evidence mappings, projection diffs, segmented journa"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"ls and 100k-event replay.\n- The router is write-denied by default. Worker submissions validate ticke"},{"id":"p13s6","text":"t revisions, input digests and the live workspace lease epoch; the watchdog quarantines unknown side"},{"id":"p13s7","text":" effects and restores quarantine from events.\n- Upgrades the verified host to DSH `0.2.1-rc.5` and `"},{"id":"p13s8","text":"pi-ai@1.5.0`. The upstream OpenAI catalog still reports 272k for `gpt-6.1-sol`, so the accurate 1.05"},{"id":"p13s9","text":"M profile override remains; 272k is a long-context pricing threshold, not the model limit.\n- The sub"},{"id":"p13s10","text":"scription compatibility build is based on `dsh-plugin-subscriptions@0.9.12` and retains the Claude e"},{"id":"p13s11","text":"mpty-block and Gemini 4 Argon fixes. Local rc.5 plugin builds declare and test the exact host versio"},{"id":"p13s12","text":"ty-block and Gemini 4 Argon fixes. Local rc.5 plugin builds declare and test the exact host version."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### What's new in 3.2.1"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"- Fixed large sessions that switched to a smaller-context model and then returned only reasoning wit"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"h a length stop. Route admission now uses DSH's native `ctx.tokenMeter`, `contextWindow`, and `defau"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"ltMaxTokens`, skips unsafe routes, and fails before dispatch when no candidate can hold the session."},{"id":"p15s4","text":"\n- 3.2.1 initially consumed the host declaration for OpenAI models. 3.2.1 later proved that the host"},{"id":"p15s5","text":"'s `272000` value was the long-context price boundary for direct GPT-6 models; 3.3.1 corrects that m"},{"id":"p15s6","text":"etadata while keeping Codex and third-party provider limits separate.\n- The release states the real "},{"id":"p15s7","text":"3.2.0 boundary: its core modules exist, but the full runtime migration is not complete. Native ask-u"},{"id":"p15s8","text":"ser, todo, time context, workspace instructions, jobs, goal, plan mode, and Git worktree remain host"},{"id":"p15s9","text":"do, time context, workspace instructions, jobs, goal, plan mode, and Git worktree remain host-owned."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### What's new in 3.2.0"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"- Expert cards are collapsed by default and expand independently to show primary, fallback and upgra"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"de routes; invalid saved drafts reopen automatically.\n- Official and third-party Jev sources are mut"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"ually exclusive. Third-party mode uses catalog-backed provider/model/reasoning selectors, never asks"},{"id":"p17s4","text":" for a model ID and does not read the official API key.\n- Managed editing experts use the native DSH"},{"id":"p17s5","text":" Git worktree tool. A worktree is bound to one ticket/assignment, cannot be reused across tickets, s"},{"id":"p17s6","text":"urvives restart as manual-recovery state, and is never auto-removed.\n- Adds Ticket lifecycle, RouteE"},{"id":"p17s7","text":"ngine, Router/Worker, event journal and Watchdog cores while retaining the existing experts, quota/a"},{"id":"p17s8","text":"uthentication/eligibility checks, fallback chains and evidence gates.\n- Adds resource and capability"},{"id":"p17s9","text":" metadata for Antigravity, DSH OpenCode Go, OpenCode and the relevant model families."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### What's new in 3.1.9"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"- Provider checkboxes let expert requests use the model default language while final host summaries "},{"id":"p19s2","text":"follow the configured output language. Explicit task language is preserved.\n- Language policy follow"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"s the actual provider after fallback and default changes on continued sessions.\n- Subscription-pool "},{"id":"p19s4","text":"transport errors retain network recovery semantics; local cooldown messages explain how to refresh s"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"ubscription usage without claiming current quota exhaustion.\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
